{
    desc => q{J joins current line with the next line},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/join_lines_J`

Tests that the **J** command joins the current line with the line below,
adding a space between them and placing the cursor at the join point.

**Keys:** `J`

**initial.png**
- Buffer has 3 lines: "hello", "world", "foo"
- Cursor on line 1 at column 0

**after_join.png**
- Buffer has 2 lines: "hello world" and "foo"
- Cursor on the space between "hello" and "world"
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('J');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_join');
    },
}__DATA__
hello
world
foo
